@startuml
title Ticket workflow with gates G1 - G5

start
:User gives ticket ""0_ticket/<id>.rst"" to LEADER;
:LEADER creates branch ""ticket/<id>"";

repeat
  :ARCHITECT: SWE.1 requirements;
repeat while (G1: user approves requirements?) is (changes requested) not (approved)
:LEADER commits ""G1 <id>: requirements"";

repeat
  :ARCHITECT: SWE.2 architecture;
  :DESIGNER: feasibility review;
repeat while (G2: findings?) is (yes, ARCHITECT fixes\nmax 2 rounds, then ask user) not (no)
:LEADER commits ""G2 <id>: architecture"";

repeat
  :DESIGNER: SWE.3 design per component\n(1_swcReq, 2_design, 3_inc, 4_config);
  :ARCHITECT: design review;
repeat while (G3: findings?) is (yes, DESIGNER fixes) not (no)
:LEADER commits ""G3 <id>: interfaces frozen"";
note right: 3_inc and 4_config are frozen.\nPorting.h change is reported to the user.

fork
  :CODER: SWE.3 code (5_src);
fork again
  :DESIGNER: SWE.4 unit tests (6_test);
fork again
  :INTEGRATOR: SWE.5 scenarios\nand JSON data;
end fork

repeat
  :INTEGRATOR: run unitTestBuild.sh;
  :ARCHITECT: code review;
repeat while (G4: failures or findings?) is (yes, LEADER assigns fix:\ncode -> CODER, test or design -> DESIGNER) not (no)
:LEADER commits ""G4 <id>: units verified"";

repeat
  :INTEGRATOR: run integration tests,\nfull docGen.sh and unitTestBuild.sh;
  :LEADER: review build results;
repeat while (G5: tests fail, coverage < 90 %\nor new Sphinx-Needs warnings?) is (yes, LEADER assigns fix) not (no)
:LEADER commits ""G5 <id>: integrated"";

:LEADER reports to the user;
:LEADER asks whether to delete the ticket;
stop

@enduml
